menu "Example Configurations"
    config EXAMPLE_ENABLE_SD_CARD
        bool "Enable SD Card"
        default n
        help 
            Enabling this option will initialize the SD card, so the SD card needs to be inserted into the slot. Additionally, if using the Video Player example, an MJPEG format video must be saved on the SD card.
endmenu

menu "LCD Panel Selection"

choice LCD_PANEL_SELECTION
    prompt "LCD panel model"
    default LCD_PANEL_JD9366
    help
        Selects between the two supported 800x1280 MIPI-DSI panels. Both are
        2-lane portrait RGB565 modules, so the LVGL/UI layer is untouched by
        this choice.

config LCD_PANEL_JD9366
    bool "JD9366 (2-lane @1000 Mbps, DPI 80 MHz)"
    help
        800x1280 panel driven through the local esp_lcd_jd9366 component.
        The panel answers DCS ACK normally, so the IDF default behaviour is
        kept.

config LCD_PANEL_ILI9881C
    bool "ILI9881C / MX101BA2140-48C (2-lane @800 Mbps, DPI 72 MHz)"
    help
        800x1280 BOE panel driven through the local esp_lcd_ili9881c
        component. Two module quirks are handled in code:
        - it never answers DCS ACK, so ack_rqst_en is disabled after the
          DBI IO is created (otherwise the first DCS write deadlocks);
        - its vendor init sequence pins COLMOD=RGB565, so LV_COLOR_DEPTH
          must stay 16 (enforced at compile time).

endchoice

endmenu
